From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hush: command -v prints an applet's path when it is on PATH

With FEATURE_SH_STANDALONE an applet is found before PATH is searched,
so "command -v md5sum" printed "md5sum".  POSIX specifies the utility's
path name.  The common test [ -x "$(command -v md5sum)" ] therefore
failed for every applet, and fontconfig's run-test.sh stopped with "No
md5sum or equivalent command".

-v and -V now print an applet's path when the applet is installed on
PATH.  The applet still runs either way.  An applet with no file on PATH
is still reported as an applet.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted

diff --git a/shell/hush.c b/shell/hush.c
--- a/shell/hush.c
+++ b/shell/hush.c
@@ -9393,7 +9393,19 @@
 	{
 		int a = find_applet_by_name(argv[0]);
 		if (a >= 0) {
-			if_command_vV_print_and_exit(opt_vV, argv[0], "an applet");
+			/* POSIX specifies a path name for "command -v".  If
+			 * the applet is installed on PATH, print that path.
+			 * The applet runs either way.  Otherwise report it as
+			 * an applet.
+			 */
+			if (opt_vV) {
+				char *path = find_executable_in_PATH(argv[0]);
+				int on_path = path != NULL;
+
+				free(path);
+				if_command_vV_print_and_exit(opt_vV, argv[0],
+						on_path ? NULL : "an applet");
+			}
 # if BB_MMU /* see above why on NOMMU it is not allowed */
 			if (APPLET_IS_NOEXEC(a)) {
 				/* Do not leak open fds from opened script files etc.
